  "description": "JEKTOL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: 0.5(C102 H116 Cr1 Dy6 O38 1+),0.5(C101 H112 Cr1 Dy6 N1 O40),0.5(N1 O3 1-),3.5(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.458-3.788 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.56-106.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CrDy6(OH)8(ortho-tol)12(MeOH)5(NO3)]·3MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
